</tbody></table>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;text-indent:36pt;">For the fourth quarter of 2025 for the Company overall, revenue increased 73%, gross profit increased 44%, and contribution increased 47% compared to the fourth quarter of 2024.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;text-indent:36pt;">Gross margin decreased to 34.5% during the fourth quarter of 2025 compared to 41.4% during the fourth quarter of last year, with the decline in gross margin primarily attributable to the acquisition of Irwin, which historically operated at a lower gross margin than Legacy FitLife.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;text-indent:36pt;">Contribution as a percentage of revenue decreased to 29.6% compared to 34.9% during the fourth quarter of last year. Excluding the effect of the inventory step-up amortization of $653, gross margin and contribution as a percentage of revenue would have been 37.0% and 32.2%, respectively, during the fourth quarter.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

